---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
    title="A Tern node"
    description="Someone shared a Tern node with you: its address, and the code to check it by."
    noindex
>
    <section class="node wrap">
        <div id="found" hidden>
            <h1>A Tern node</h1>
            <p class="lede">Someone shared their node with you. This is its address.</p>

            <div class="card">
                <p class="label">Its code</p>
                <p id="code" class="code"></p>
                <p class="muted small">
                    Check it with them: their node shows the same twelve digits on its <strong>This node</strong> page.
                    If they differ, this is not their node.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
                <p class="label">Its address</p>
                <p id="address" class="address"></p>
                <p class="actions">
                    <button id="copy" type="button">Copy the address</button>
                    <a id="add" class="button secondary" href="/app">Add it in the app</a>
                </p>
                <p id="copied" class="muted small" role="status"></p>
            </div>

            <p class="muted small">
                To reach it, add the address as a contact: in the <a href="/apps">Tern app</a> on Android, where
                this link opens in the app, or on iPhone, iPad or Mac, by scanning its QR code or pasting the link;
                in the <a href="/app">app in your browser</a>; or with <code>contact</code> on a board's console.
                Nothing is sent to the node until you write to it.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div id="missing" hidden>
            <h1>No node here</h1>
            <p class="lede">
                This link does not hold a node's address. A node's link is the one its QR code opens, on
                its <strong>Share</strong> page; check it was not cut short.
            </p>
        </div>

        <noscript>
            <p class="lede">This page reads the node's address out of its link, which needs JavaScript.</p>
        </noscript>

        <p class="muted small privacy">
            This page reads the address out of the link in your browser and sends it nowhere. Opening the link did
            tell this site which address you looked at, as any web address does; it keeps no logs. A phone with
            the Tern app for Android opens these links in the app, without asking the site.
        </p>
    </section>
</Base>

<script>
    import "../lib/node/page.ts";
</script>

<style>
    .node {
        padding-top: 32px;
        padding-bottom: 48px;
        max-width: 40rem;
    }
    [hidden] {
        display: none !important;
    }
    h1 {
        font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
        margin: 0 0 12px;
    }
    .lede {
        font-size: 1.1rem;
    }
    .card {
        background: var(--surface);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        padding: 12px 16px;
        margin: 16px 0;
    }
    .label {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
        color: var(--muted);
    }
    .code {
        margin: 4px 0 8px;
        font: 600 clamp(1.6rem, 7vw, 2.2rem) / 1.2 ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
        font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    }
    .address {
        margin: 6px 0 12px;
        font: 1rem / 1.6 ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
        word-spacing: 0.3em;
        overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }
    .actions {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 8px;
        margin: 0;
    }
    .small {
        font-size: 0.9rem;
    }
    .privacy {
        margin-top: 28px;
    }
    button,
    a.button {
        display: inline-block;
        font: inherit;
        padding: 9px 16px;
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        border: 1px solid var(--accent);
        background: var(--accent);
        color: var(--bg);
        font-weight: 600;
        cursor: pointer;
        text-decoration: none;
    }
    a.button.secondary {
        background: transparent;
        color: var(--accent);
    }
</style>
